=======================================
 MacIP link layer module for Marinetti
Copyright (c) 1998-2003 Richard Bennett
    Written by Richard Bennett
=======================================

This file contains the change history for the MacIP link layer module.

People who assisted with new information on a bug are listed in brackets.

  1.2 - 23rd July 2003

- Bumped version number

  1.2d3 - 10th November 2002

- Debug output in format acceptable to Text2Pcap (Andrew)

  1.1 - 29th March 2002

- Released as open source.

  1.1a1 - 9th July 1999

- Support for LinkConfigFileName. Filename = MacIP.config

  1.0 - release

  1.0b5 -

- Couple of changes now that I actually have an "AppleShare Programmer's Guide
  for the Apple II" reference. Mainly source level only, but test to be sure.
  There's nothing that should improve the datagrams not getting through
  problem.

  1.0b4 - 16th August 1998

- Now uses link layer interface version 2, which requires Marinetti 2.1.
- Was trashing Marinetti's direct page. Left over from the original hack at
  Tony's, when I was doing a dodgey by doubling up on direct page I knew
  wasn't being used. Marinetti 2.0f4 moved its direct page around, causing it
  to get confused about some new pointers which suddenly appeared out of
  nowhere! Fixed. Now only uses direct page space allocated per link layer
  module specification.
- Connect message flag was being read as reversed, causing messages when
  not, and not when messages. Fixed.

  1.0b3 - 14th August 1998

- If show connect messages was turned on, but display pointer was nil, MacIP
  was still trying to call address $00/0000. Dumb, really dumb... Fixed.

  1.0b2 - 9th August 1998

- For some reason the memory userid wasn't being set up, causing all memory
  allocations to fail. Fixed.

  1.0b1 - 8th August 1998

- Added a boot icon. I don't really like it much, feel free to mess with it.
  (Requires Marinetti 2.0f3 to display the icon on boot)

  1.0a3 - 7th August 1998

- Stack imbalance in new datagram build routine. (I don't have access to a
  network, so testing involves emailing Tony with each new build)
- Optimised datagram build routine.
- Now returns authorisation messages on connect errors.
- Now correctly cleans up after a failed connect.

  1.0a2 - 7th August 1998

- Was trashing random locations in bank 0 (bad DP register) while building
  incoming datagrams. This has been in since day one. Fixed.
  (Tony Diaz)

  1.0a1 - 7th August 1998

- Changed dialog layout to be more intuitive.
- Re-organising source now that I have access to my macros and documentation.
- rVersion bytes were in the wrong order. Fixed. Requires Marinetti 2.0f3 to
  display correctly on text boot splash.

  1.0d6 - 1st August to 3rd August 1998

- Initial release. Developed at Tony Diaz' place.

*END*
